---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro'
import DownloadCard from '@/components/DownloadCard.astro'
import { release, formattedReleaseDate } from '@/data/release'
import { site } from '@/data/site'
---

<Base
  title="Download Notch for Windows — unsigned, verified"
  description="Download the latest Notch build for Windows 10 and 11. Installer or portable, SHA-256 checksums published, no account required."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Download</span>
      <h1>Download Notch for Windows.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        One file, no account. Choose the installer for a Start-menu shortcut, or the portable build
        if you would rather not install anything.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" style="padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px)">
    <div style="margin-top: 32px">
      <DownloadCard />
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>If Windows warns you</h2>
      <p>
        SmartScreen shows “Windows protected your PC”. Choose <strong>More info</strong>, then
        <strong>Run anyway</strong>. This appears because the build is unsigned, not because
        anything was detected. The same file is produced by the public workflow in the repository.
      </p>

      <h2>If Smart App Control blocks it</h2>
      <p>
        Smart App Control on Windows 11 refuses unsigned apps. Try the portable build first. If that
        is blocked too, Notch cannot run without changing that setting — and turning it off weakens
        protection for everything on the PC, so decide deliberately.
      </p>

      <h2>After installing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Hover the top centre of the screen. The notch unfolds.</li>
        <li>Press Esc, or use the collapse arrow, to fold it back.</li>
        <li>Turn on posture only if you want it; the camera is requested at that moment.</li>
        <li>Spotify Desktop is picked up automatically. A full connection is optional.</li>
        <li>Set <strong>Launch at login</strong> in Settings if you want it always available.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Uninstall</h2>
      <p>
        Settings → Apps → Notch. Notes in your folder are untouched. Delete
        <code>%APPDATA%\notch</code> to remove settings, logs and Spotify tokens as well.
      </p>

      <h2>Stay current</h2>
      <p>
        Notch does not auto-update. The latest version is <strong>{release.version}</strong>, released
        {formattedReleaseDate}. Every build is listed on
        <a href={site.releasesUrl} rel="noopener">GitHub releases</a>, and the
        <a href="/changelog">changelog</a> explains what changed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
